IMPORT prelude
IMPORT `coa-definitions`

-- Companies Act 1967 (Singapore) -- sections 5, 5A, 5B and 6: subsidiary, holding
-- company, ultimate holding company, wholly owned subsidiary, and related
-- corporation.
--
-- These four sections are what 154 other Acts mean when they say "subsidiary",
-- "holding company" or "related corporation" without defining it.
--
-- NAIVE ENCODING. Straight from the deposited text with the writing-l4-rules
-- skill. No pipeline, no coverage table, no independent test pass, no human gate.
--
-- THE MODEL. A group is a list of direct control links, each saying whether one named
-- corporation controls another by one of the two routes in s 5(1)(a). The links are
-- taken as COMPLETE: a relationship not in the list does not exist. s 5(1)(b) makes
-- "subsidiary" transitive, which the encoding follows through the list; the
-- recursion is bounded by the number of links so a cyclic group cannot loop.

§ `Companies Act 1967 -- ss 5, 5A, 5B and 6`

§§ `5(1)(a), 5(2) -- control of the board`

-- s 5(2): "the composition of a corporation's board of directors is deemed to be
-- controlled by another corporation if that other corporation BY THE EXERCISE OF SOME
-- POWER EXERCISABLE BY IT WITHOUT THE CONSENT OR CONCURRENCE OF ANY OTHER PERSON can
-- appoint or remove ALL OR A MAJORITY of the directors, and for the purposes of this
-- provision that other corporation is DEEMED TO HAVE POWER TO MAKE SUCH AN
-- APPOINTMENT if --
--   (a) a person cannot be appointed as a director without the exercise in his or her
--       favour by that other corporation of such a power; or
--   (b) a person's appointment as a director follows necessarily from his or her
--       being a director or other officer of that other corporation."
--
-- The deeming is of the power to MAKE AN APPOINTMENT, not of the power to remove, and
-- it is expressed person by person ("a person cannot be appointed ..."), while the
-- control test is "all or a majority". The encoding reads limbs (a) and (b) as
-- applying to a majority of the directors, which is the only reading under which
-- they bear on the control test; a single director appointed by the parent under (a)
-- would not by itself make a parent of the corporation. That is a reading.
DECLARE HolderKind IS ONE OF
    `the parent itself`
    `a nominee of the parent`
    `a subsidiary of the parent`
    `a nominee of a subsidiary of the parent`
    `someone else`

-- s 5(1)(a)(ii): "controls more than half of the voting power". s 5(3) says which
-- shares and which power count, and the five rules are carried on each holding.
DECLARE Holding HAS
    `held by` IS A HolderKind
    `voting power, as a percentage of all the voting power in the child` IS A NUMBER
    `held or exercisable only in a fiduciary capacity by the parent or by the subsidiary concerned` IS A BOOLEAN
    `held by virtue of the provisions of debentures of the child or of a trust deed securing them` IS A BOOLEAN
    `held by way of security only, for a transaction in the ordinary course of a lending business of the parent or the subsidiary` IS A BOOLEAN

DECLARE Control HAS
    `the parent` IS A STRING
    `the child` IS A STRING
    `the parent is a corporation within section 4(1)` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the child is a corporation within section 4(1)` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the parent can appoint or remove all or a majority of the directors by a power exercisable without anyone else's consent` IS A BOOLEAN
    `a majority of the directors cannot be appointed without the parent exercising such a power in their favour` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the appointment of a majority of the directors follows necessarily from their being directors or officers of the parent` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the holdings in the child` IS A LIST OF Holding

DECLARE Group HAS
    `the links` IS A LIST OF Control

§§ `5(3) -- which shares and which power are counted`

-- s 5(3): "In determining whether one corporation is a subsidiary of another
-- corporation --
--   (a) any shares held or power exercisable by that other corporation in a FIDUCIARY
--       CAPACITY is to be treated as NOT held or exercisable by it;
--   (b) subject to paragraphs (c) and (d), any shares held or power exercisable --
--       (i) by any person as a NOMINEE for that other corporation (except where that
--           other corporation is concerned only in a fiduciary capacity); or
--       (ii) by, or by a nominee for, a SUBSIDIARY of that other corporation, not
--            being a subsidiary which is concerned only in a fiduciary capacity,
--       is to be treated as held or exercisable by that other corporation;
--   (c) any shares held or power exercisable by any person BY VIRTUE OF THE PROVISIONS
--       OF ANY DEBENTURES of the firstmentioned corporation or of a TRUST DEED for
--       securing any issue of such debentures is to be DISREGARDED; and
--   (d) any shares held or power exercisable by, or by a nominee for, that other
--       corporation or its subsidiary (not being held or exercisable as mentioned in
--       paragraph (c)) is to be treated as NOT held or exercisable by that other
--       corporation if the ordinary business of that other corporation or its
--       subsidiary includes the LENDING OF MONEY and the shares are held ... by way
--       of security only for the purposes of a transaction entered into in the
--       ordinary course of that business."
--
-- THE CIRCULARITY. Limb (b)(ii) counts shares held by "a subsidiary of that other
-- corporation". Whether a corporation is a subsidiary of the parent is the very
-- question s 5(1) is answering, so determining whether C is a subsidiary of P can
-- depend on whether S is a subsidiary of P, which can depend on C. The Act gives no
-- order of determination. The encoding avoids the loop by taking the status of the
-- holder as a supplied fact (the holder kind), and records the circularity in NOTES.md.
GIVEN `the holding` IS A Holding
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the holding counts towards the parent's voting power` IF
        NOT (`the holding`'s `held by` EQUALS `someone else`)
    AND NOT `the holding`'s `held or exercisable only in a fiduciary capacity by the parent or by the subsidiary concerned`
    AND NOT `the holding`'s `held by virtue of the provisions of debentures of the child or of a trust deed securing them`
    AND NOT `the holding`'s `held by way of security only, for a transaction in the ordinary course of a lending business of the parent or the subsidiary`

GIVEN `the holdings` IS A LIST OF Holding
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `the voting power that counts` IS
    CONSIDER `the holdings`
    WHEN EMPTY THEN 0
    WHEN `h` FOLLOWED BY `rest`
        THEN (IF `the holding counts towards the parent's voting power` `h`
              THEN `h`'s `voting power, as a percentage of all the voting power in the child`
              ELSE 0)
             PLUS `the voting power that counts` `rest`

§§ `5(1)(a) -- direct control`

GIVEN `the link` IS A Control
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the parent controls the composition of the board` IF
        `the link`'s `the parent can appoint or remove all or a majority of the directors by a power exercisable without anyone else's consent`
    OR  `the link`'s `a majority of the directors cannot be appointed without the parent exercising such a power in their favour`
    OR  `the link`'s `the appointment of a majority of the directors follows necessarily from their being directors or officers of the parent`

-- s 5(1)(a)(ii): MORE than half. At exactly 50% neither of two joint-venture parents
-- controls the voting power, and unless one of them controls the board neither is a
-- holding company.
GIVEN `the link` IS A Control
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the parent controls more than half of the voting power` IF
    `the voting power that counts` (`the link`'s `the holdings in the child`) GREATER THAN 50

-- Both bodies have to be "corporations" for the purposes of the Act. A company wholly
-- owned by a cooperative society, a registered trade union or a limited liability
-- partnership is therefore not its subsidiary, because those are outside the
-- definition of "corporation" in s 4(1).
GIVEN `the link` IS A Control
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the child is a direct subsidiary of the parent` IF
        `the link`'s `the parent is a corporation within section 4(1)`
    AND `the link`'s `the child is a corporation within section 4(1)`
    AND (    `the parent controls the composition of the board` `the link`
         OR  `the parent controls more than half of the voting power` `the link`)

§§ `5(1)(b) -- a subsidiary of a subsidiary is a subsidiary`

GIVEN `the links` IS A LIST OF Control
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `the number of links` IS
    CONSIDER `the links`
    WHEN EMPTY THEN 0
    WHEN `l` FOLLOWED BY `rest` THEN 1 PLUS `the number of links` `rest`

-- Is there, among the links still to be looked at, one from `the parent` that is a
-- direct subsidiary relationship, and whose child is the target or a subsidiary of
-- the target? `the group` carries the whole list so each step can start again from
-- the top, and the list being walked comes last in the parameters.
GIVEN `the parent` IS A STRING,
      `the target` IS A STRING,
      `fuel` IS A NUMBER,
      `the group` IS A Group,
      `the remaining links` IS A LIST OF Control
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `a chain of control leads from the parent to the target` IS
    CONSIDER `the remaining links`
    WHEN EMPTY THEN FALSE
    WHEN `l` FOLLOWED BY `rest`
        THEN     (    `l`'s `the parent` EQUALS `the parent`
                  AND `the child is a direct subsidiary of the parent` `l`
                  AND (    `l`'s `the child` EQUALS `the target`
                       OR  (    `fuel` GREATER THAN 0
                            AND `a chain of control leads from the parent to the target` (`l`'s `the child`) `the target` (`fuel` MINUS 1) `the group` (`the group`'s `the links`))))
             OR  `a chain of control leads from the parent to the target` `the parent` `the target` `fuel` `the group` `rest`

GIVEN `the group` IS A Group, `the parent` IS A STRING, `the target` IS A STRING
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the target is a subsidiary of the parent` IF
    `a chain of control leads from the parent to the target` `the parent` `the target` (`the number of links` (`the group`'s `the links`)) `the group` (`the group`'s `the links`)

-- s 5(4): "A reference in this Act to the holding company of a company or other
-- corporation is a reference to a corporation of which that last mentioned company or
-- corporation is a subsidiary." So holding company is the converse of subsidiary and
-- is just as transitive: every corporation up the chain is a holding company.
GIVEN `the group` IS A Group, `the candidate` IS A STRING, `the company` IS A STRING
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the candidate is a holding company of the company` IF
    `the target is a subsidiary of the parent` `the group` `the candidate` `the company`

-- s 5(5): "the Depository is not to be regarded as a holding company of a corporation by
-- reason only of the shares it holds in that corporation as a bare trustee."
GIVEN `its only connection with the corporation is shares it holds as a bare trustee` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the Depository is regarded as a holding company of the corporation` IF
    NOT `its only connection with the corporation is shares it holds as a bare trustee`

§§ `5A -- ultimate holding company`

-- s 5A: "a corporation is the ultimate holding company of another corporation if --
--   (a) the other corporation is a subsidiary of the firstmentioned corporation; and
--   (b) the firstmentioned corporation is NOT ITSELF A SUBSIDIARY of any corporation."
--
-- Limb (b) quantifies over "any corporation", so the group has to be complete. A
-- corporation is a subsidiary of some corporation exactly when it is the child of a
-- direct subsidiary relationship somewhere in the list (the last link of any chain is
-- a direct one).
GIVEN `the name` IS A STRING, `the remaining links` IS A LIST OF Control
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `some link makes the named corporation a direct subsidiary` IS
    CONSIDER `the remaining links`
    WHEN EMPTY THEN FALSE
    WHEN `l` FOLLOWED BY `rest`
        THEN     (`l`'s `the child` EQUALS `the name` AND `the child is a direct subsidiary of the parent` `l`)
             OR  `some link makes the named corporation a direct subsidiary` `the name` `rest`

GIVEN `the group` IS A Group, `the candidate` IS A STRING, `the company` IS A STRING
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the candidate is the ultimate holding company of the company` IF
        `the target is a subsidiary of the parent` `the group` `the candidate` `the company`
    AND NOT `some link makes the named corporation a direct subsidiary` `the candidate` (`the group`'s `the links`)

§§ `5B -- wholly owned subsidiary`

-- s 5B: "a corporation is a wholly owned subsidiary of another corporation if NONE OF
-- THE MEMBERS of the firstmentioned corporation is a person other than --
--   (a) that other corporation;
--   (b) a nominee of that other corporation;
--   (c) a subsidiary of that other corporation BEING A SUBSIDIARY NONE OF THE MEMBERS
--       OF WHICH IS A PERSON OTHER THAN THAT OTHER CORPORATION OR A NOMINEE OF THAT
--       OTHER CORPORATION; or
--   (d) a nominee of such subsidiary."
--
-- THIS SECTION IS NOT TRANSITIVE, AND THAT MATTERS. Limb (c) admits a subsidiary as a
-- member only if ITS OWN members are the parent or the parent's nominees. It admits no
-- subsidiary whose members are themselves intermediate subsidiaries. So in a chain
--     P --100%--> S2 --100%--> S1 --100%--> C
-- the corporation C has a single member, S1. S1 is a subsidiary of P, but S1's only
-- member is S2, "a person other than" P or P's nominee. So S1 fails limb (c) and C is
-- NOT a wholly owned subsidiary of P, although every share in the chain is held by
-- the one group. C is a wholly owned subsidiary of S1, and S1 of S2, and S2 of P, but
-- s 5B contains no equivalent of s 5(1)(b) to carry the status upwards.
--
-- The evident intention was almost certainly otherwise. The encoding follows the words
-- and asserts the three-tier chain as the case where they part from the intention.
DECLARE Occupant IS ONE OF
    `the other corporation itself`
    `a nominee of the other corporation`
    `a subsidiary of the other corporation`
    `a nominee of a subsidiary of the other corporation`
    `any other person`

GIVEN `who` IS AN Occupant
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the occupant is the other corporation or its nominee` IF
    CONSIDER `who`
    WHEN `the other corporation itself` THEN TRUE
    WHEN `a nominee of the other corporation` THEN TRUE
    OTHERWISE FALSE

DECLARE Member HAS
    `who it is` IS AN Occupant
    `the members of the subsidiary concerned` IS A LIST OF Occupant

GIVEN `the occupants` IS A LIST OF Occupant
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `every occupant is the other corporation or its nominee` IS
    CONSIDER `the occupants`
    WHEN EMPTY THEN TRUE
    WHEN `o` FOLLOWED BY `rest`
        THEN     `the occupant is the other corporation or its nominee` `o`
             AND `every occupant is the other corporation or its nominee` `rest`

GIVEN `the member` IS A Member
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `this member is one that section 5B allows` IF
    CONSIDER `the member`'s `who it is`
    WHEN `the other corporation itself` THEN TRUE
    WHEN `a nominee of the other corporation` THEN TRUE
    WHEN `a subsidiary of the other corporation`
        THEN `every occupant is the other corporation or its nominee` (`the member`'s `the members of the subsidiary concerned`)
    WHEN `a nominee of a subsidiary of the other corporation`
        THEN `every occupant is the other corporation or its nominee` (`the member`'s `the members of the subsidiary concerned`)
    OTHERWISE FALSE

GIVEN `the members` IS A LIST OF Member
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `every member is one that section 5B allows` IS
    CONSIDER `the members`
    WHEN EMPTY THEN TRUE
    WHEN `m` FOLLOWED BY `rest`
        THEN     `this member is one that section 5B allows` `m`
             AND `every member is one that section 5B allows` `rest`

-- The Act says "a subsidiary of that other corporation", so the corporation must
-- first be a subsidiary at all (it cannot be wholly owned without being one).
GIVEN `the group` IS A Group,
      `the parent` IS A STRING,
      `the child` IS A STRING,
      `the members of the child` IS A LIST OF Member
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the child is a wholly owned subsidiary of the parent` IF
        `every member is one that section 5B allows` `the members of the child`
    AND `the target is a subsidiary of the parent` `the group` `the parent` `the child`

§§ `6 -- related corporations`

-- s 6: "Where a corporation --
--   (a) is the holding company of another corporation;
--   (b) is a subsidiary of another corporation; or
--   (c) is a subsidiary of the holding company of another corporation,
-- that firstmentioned corporation and that other corporation are for the purposes of
-- this Act deemed to be related to each other."
--
-- Limb (c) makes two subsidiaries of a common holding company related, and
-- "holding company" is transitive by s 5(4). So any two corporations that share a
-- holding company anywhere above them are related: cousins at different depths of one
-- group are related to each other as much as sisters. The holding company has to be a
-- corporation that appears as a parent in the group, and the loop walks the parents.
GIVEN `the group` IS A Group, `the first` IS A STRING, `the second` IS A STRING, `the remaining links` IS A LIST OF Control
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `they share a holding company in the links` IS
    CONSIDER `the remaining links`
    WHEN EMPTY THEN FALSE
    WHEN `l` FOLLOWED BY `rest`
        THEN     (    `the candidate is a holding company of the company` `the group` (`l`'s `the parent`) `the first`
                  AND `the candidate is a holding company of the company` `the group` (`l`'s `the parent`) `the second`)
             OR  `they share a holding company in the links` `the group` `the first` `the second` `rest`

GIVEN `the group` IS A Group, `the first` IS A STRING, `the second` IS A STRING
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the first and the second are related corporations` IF
        `the candidate is a holding company of the company` `the group` `the first` `the second`
    OR  `the candidate is a holding company of the company` `the group` `the second` `the first`
    OR  `they share a holding company in the links` `the group` `the first` `the second` (`the group`'s `the links`)
